{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The great luminaries.</b> Rashi explained: they were created equal. One may say: from that time onward they were equal in their circle (orb), even though their light was not the same. Rashi further explained: and the moon was diminished. One may say: this means it diminishes from full moon until the new moon. And Rashi further explained: it is impossible for two kings to use one crown — the meaning is, it is inconceivable that the sun and I should shine equally in our circle; so the moon thought that the sun should be diminished." "<b>The great ones.</b> Named so relative to the stars, which are smaller than all of them." "<b>For dominion of the day.</b> Over the fruits — to ripen them." "<b>For dominion of the night.</b> To cool things, so they do not become maggoty. But for the light that was created on the first day, the term dominion does not apply, for it does not rule to produce fruits."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:27.050735488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}